# Settings for the LAN watch party stack (docs: LAN watch party).
#
# `./scripts/provision-lan.sh --init` copies this file to `.env.lan` (git-ignored, owner-only) with a random database
# password, and creates `.env.lan.auth` and `.env.lan.idempotency`: new keys, never the dev ones. Fill in the
# required values below, then start the stack from the repository root:
#   docker compose -f infra/compose/docker-compose.lan.yml --env-file infra/compose/.env.lan up -d --build --wait

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Password for the LAN database (`--init` generates one).
PVPICKS_DB_PASSWORD=
# The name phones open, without https://: lan.p2picks.com. Its DNS A record (Cloudflare, proxy off) points at this Mac's
# LAN address. For a test on this Mac only, use localhost with PVPICKS_LAN_TLS=internal.
PVPICKS_LAN_HOST=
# The admin account to create on first start, and its password (the admin portal's password: 12 to 64 characters,
# not containing the username, not a common password). Players have no passwords: each gets a sign-in code the admin
# shows as a QR code. The admin can't play: create yourself a player account too.
PVPICKS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN=
PVPICKS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- Sports data ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BallDontLie API key (All-Star for NBA and NFL). Without it there are no games.
PVPICKS_BALLDONTLIE_API_KEY=
# All-Star request budget (60 a minute); lower these only for a smaller plan.
# PVPICKS_SPORTS_POLL_INTERVAL=PT15S
# PVPICKS_SPORTS_STATS_INTERVAL=PT3S

# --- HTTPS ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the certificate obtained before the party lives (fullchain.pem and privkey.pem). Git-ignored by default.
# PVPICKS_LAN_CERT_DIR=../caddy/certs
# "internal" uses Caddy's own CA instead: fine for testing on this Mac, but phones won't trust it.
# PVPICKS_LAN_TLS=/certs/fullchain.pem /certs/privkey.pem
